// Conn and ServerConn local_addr, remote_addr and close_write (decision
// 0644 T11; Go's net.Conn LocalAddr, RemoteAddr and TCPConn.CloseWrite,
// tls_test.go TestConnCloseWrite's shape): a client shuts its sending
// side, the server reads to the end of the stream and answers on the
// still open other half; the two ends' addresses mirror each other.
fn main(os: Os) {
  let l = os.net.listen("127.0.0.1:0").or_fault("listen")
  scope s {
    let srv = s.spawn(fn() -> Str {
      let c = l.accept().or_fault("accept")
      var n = 0
      while let Some(b) = c.read(4096).or_fault("server read") {
        n = n + b.len()
      }
      c.write("got ${n}".bytes()).or_fault("server write")
      let addrs = "${c.local_addr() == l.addr()} ${c.remote_addr().starts_with("127.0.0.1:")}"
      c.close_write().or_fault("server close_write")
      c.close()
      addrs
    })
    let c = os.net.dial(l.addr()).or_fault("dial")
    os.stdio.println("client remote is the listener: ${c.remote_addr() == l.addr()}")
    os.stdio.println("client local: ${c.local_addr().starts_with("127.0.0.1:")} ${c.local_addr() != c.remote_addr()}")
    c.write(b"hello, half closed").or_fault("write")
    c.close_write().or_fault("close_write")
    match c.write(b"more") {
      Ok(_) => os.stdio.println("write after close_write: ok")
      Err(_) => os.stdio.println("write after close_write: fails")
    }
    var got = b""
    while let Some(b) = c.read(4096).or_fault("read") {
      got = got + b
    }
    os.stdio.println("reply: ${got.to_str_lossy()}")
    os.stdio.println("server: ${srv.await}")
    c.close()
  }
  os.stdio.println("done")
}
